[size=200][b]UTTchain[/b][/size]
[size=120]Unified Trading Terminal • Robinhood Chain Protocol Layer[/size][/center]

[b]UTTchain[/b] is a protocol and infrastructure project being developed for the [b]Unified Trading Terminal (UTT)[/b] and [b]Unified Trading Terminal Token (UTTT)[/b], built around Robinhood Chain.

The project is being designed [b]onchain-first[/b]. Robinhood Chain should carry deterministic protocol logic, identity, authorization, settlement, and publicly verifiable state wherever EVM execution is technically suitable and economically reasonable.

[b]No-local-companion rule[/b]

UTTchain production use must [b]not[/b] require users to run a second always-on local server, daemon, or companion machine.

The architecture priority is:

[list=1]
[*][b]Robinhood Chain smart contracts and chain state[/b]
[*][b]Browser-side execution and wallet interaction[/b]
[*][b]Replaceable RPC, oracle, and indexer infrastructure[/b]
[*][b]Hosted/serverless services only where technically unavoidable[/b]
[/list]

Existing local UTT may remain an independent application and integration surface, but it will not be a required runtime dependency for UTTchain's web/onchain protocol functions.

Smart contracts cannot directly run a browser interface, securely retain centralized-exchange API secrets, or make arbitrary authenticated HTTP requests to external exchanges. Where a workload cannot safely or technically execute inside the EVM, UTTchain will prefer browser execution, cryptographically verifiable data delivery, or replaceable hosted/serverless infrastructure rather than requiring localhost software from the user.

[b]Visual identity[/b]

The UTTchain visual system represents [b]many markets → one terminal → one protocol[/b] through a shared network/routing motif.

